00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.160
Yesterday we briefly discussed this story
on the bonus show and in the hours following

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.160
the recording of yesterday's bonus show, the
story has exploded now with corroboration.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.750
So let me kind of tell you what's going on
here.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.750
And it is.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.750
It's wild.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:21.599
A staffer for Georgia's Secretary of state,
Brad Raffensperger, said yesterday that on

00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:27.699
a phone call with Republican Senator Lindsey
Graham, Lindsey asked, could state officials

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:32.210
throw out some ballots to help Donald Trump
win the state of Georgia?

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.640
This is not an anonymous source.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.210
This is election implementation manager Gabriel
Sterling, who has come forward and said, yeah,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.469
I heard the same thing that Brad Raffensperger
heard.

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:44.750
So this is now corroboration.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:50.650
The story, as we knew it yesterday morning
was that Georgia Secretary of State Brad Raffensperger

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:58.690
said, you know, I had a phone call with Lindsey
Graham and Lindsey Graham seemed to be implying,

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.430
let's see if you can throw out some ballots.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:07.020
And he was referring, of course, to absentee
ballots, which skew heavily in favor of President

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.440
Joe Biden in the state of Georgia, as is the
case in many states.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.400
So that was the initial claim from Brad Raffensperger.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.430
Lindsey denied the claim, saying, it's ridiculous,
I didn't do it.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.370
I wasn't trying to get ballots thrown out
or anything like it, even though Raffensperger

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:28.220
seemed very, very clear about what he heard
from Lindsey Graham, Lindsey Graham saying,

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:33.750
hey, you know, if there was political bias,
maybe poll workers accepted ballots that they

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.840
shouldn't have.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.520
What if we find some ballots and we identify
some counties and we toss them out if we find

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.810
that there's a high rate of non matching signatures?

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:48.550
And Raffensperger reported being stunned that
Lindsey Graham was suggesting this and said

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:52.490
it sure seemed as though Lindsey Graham was
trying to go down that road.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.430
So that was the initial claim and Lindsey
Graham denied it.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.970
And then now, again, Gabriel Sterling has
said, I was on that phone call.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.980
I heard the exact same thing from Lindsey
Graham.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.650
So we found the attempted voter fraud.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.350
Guys, the calls are coming from inside the
house.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.780
It's Lindsey Graham saying, how about we tossed
some ballots in the trash?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:17.760
Graham has said all along, oh, I was trying
to find out how does Georgia election law

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.760
work?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.260
Does anybody believe that?

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.800
And Graham also, when asked about this, said
the president didn't urge me to do this.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.320
Now, that's one of those meaningless political
statements that it could.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.130
The letter of that could be true.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.310
But in spirit, it might be a complete and
total lie.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.640
When Lindsey Graham said, I mean, listen,
maybe Lindsey Graham came up with this idea

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.990
on his own, maybe Donald Trump came up with
the idea.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.960
But Lindsey Graham might well be right by
the letter that Trump never heard.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:53.050
Trump never called Lindsey and said, listen,
call Georgia, ask them to throw ballots in

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.210
the trash.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:03:00.740
The way these things would work is that a
Trump staffer suggests to Lindsey Graham what

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.069
would happen if you were to get on the phone
with Brad Raffensperger and see what they

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:07.740
might be able to do.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:13.210
This is like, you know, in Argentina and other
countries, my experiences with Argentina,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.440
sometimes there are corrupt police in Argentina.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:21.260
And, you know, you might get pulled over and
a police officer starts with, oh, you know,

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:26.790
not only were you speeding, but I think that
your brake light is messed up.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.670
And I think that there's too much pollution
coming from your tailpipe.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:30.670
I don't know.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.880
I might have to get back up down here.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.680
And, you know, and then you said the code.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.770
You don't say, can I bribe you?

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:39.770
Right.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.510
You say, wow, that's really inconvenient.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:46.260
Is there some other way I might be able to
resolve this today?

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.430
Could we figure out a way to resolve this
right now?

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.840
And then this game is played of, well, what
did you have in mind or the right?

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.840
Right.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.240
That's the way politics is done.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.000
It's not Lindsey, it's Donald.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.750
Tell them to throw ballots out.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.610
So Lindsey saying he wasn't urged by Trump
is completely meaningless.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.220
Now, is this illegal?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.790
I actually don't know.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.520
I mean, is the suggestion from Lindsey Graham,
if it were proven, is it against the law?

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.910
It sounds like it should be, but I really
don't know.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.340
And you just.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:22.460
Had to know that once Republicans started
screeching about voter fraud, it was them

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.880
who they were the ones who were going to try
to commit it, its projection.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.870
And many people have written to me saying
David Brat Raffensperger is a Republican.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.830
Why is he why is he going public and throwing
Lindsay Graham under the bus?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:40.750
Yeah, Raffensperger is a Republican, but he
probably realizes there's really no way to

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.270
just throw out large batches of legal ballots.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:49.020
Even if he had an idea of how he might be
able to throw out some batches of ballots,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:54.530
Braford or probably realizes that the risks
dramatically outweigh the rewards, especially

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:59.750
since flipping Georgia, if he was able to
do it, wouldn't actually give Donald Trump

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.790
a presidential win in the Electoral College.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:07.900
And in order for Raffensperger to get himself
out of possible trouble, maybe he's decided

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.370
to just go public and throw Lindsay Graham
under the bus.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.190
Now, there's one other possibility.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.370
Maybe Raffensperger is just acting with integrity
instead of hyper partizanship.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:20.639
I'm so conditioned not to assume that that
I'm mentioning that second.

00:05:20.639 --> 00:05:24.060
But it's conceivable that Raffensperger is
just acting with integrity here.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.570
Now, one other thing.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:29.530
We and others are calling this the real voter
fraud.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.090
This really isn't voter fraud.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:35.740
This is election fraud, which is the real
fraud we have to worry about.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:40.670
Voter fraud is this retail strategy that Republicans
and Trump have been crying about, someone

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:45.680
trying to vote twice, someone showing up and
saying, I'm giving the name of a dead person

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.870
and casting a ballot or submitting a bunch
of fake absentee ballots.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.070
That's really inefficient.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:53.930
Those are stupid ways to try to steal an election.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:59.580
What we're talking about here is election
fraud, which is abusing the law, trying to

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.370
do mass disenfranchisement of voters.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:08.220
This includes stuff like using weak signature
laws to throw out votes from people with maybe

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.440
black sounding names or Hispanic sounding
names or whatever it may be, people from poor

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:17.050
areas intimidating people at the polls, doing
voter purges.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.449
That's election fraud.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:20.350
And that's really the concern.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:24.250
And if this is true about Lindsey Graham,
what is being alleged?

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.240
It should be career ending.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.540
It should be indictment garden garnering,
to be perfectly frank.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.610
But nothing matters anymore to this party.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.390
And more than likely, Lindsey Graham is going
to get away with this.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:57.520
I hope I'm wrong, but I think he will get

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:49.409
away 
with it.

